// Two blooms in two trenches at two cliffs, each cut by its cliff at a different distance; a rising ember guards the second trench.
name Confluence
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 3
hint Three generations of bloom from a stone on each trench floor, cut short by each cliff. One seed lies on the road ahead, the other on the first terrace, past an ember. The blooms are the stairs.
tip A whole bloom is seven wide. A bloom five wide met the cliff: its stone is three from the open edge and one from the wall. A bloom six wide: three from the open edge, two from the wall.
intro Two springs at the feet of two cliffs, each cut short by the rock it grew against. The cliffs are the way on, and the springs are the only stairs.
outro You planted the seeds where the springs rose, and the world grew back around you. Deeper in, something is still burning.
